# Read by GitHub's "Cite this repository" widget, cffconvert and Software Heritage.
#
# Zenodo does NOT read this file: when .zenodo.json is present it is used alone and
# CITATION.cff is ignored entirely. The two must therefore be kept in agreement by
# hand — tests/test_app_version.py asserts that `version` here equals the version
# the code reports, and that .zenodo.json parses.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below. If you used the
  curated mapping dataset it produces, cite that separately — it is a different Zenodo
  record with its own DOI (10.5281/zenodo.20184643).
type: software
title: >-
  Molecular AOP Builder: curator-in-the-loop mapping of AOP Key Events to
  WikiPathways, Gene Ontology and Reactome
abstract: >-
  A curator-in-the-loop web application for building molecular Adverse Outcome
  Pathways. Candidate WikiPathways pathways, Gene Ontology Biological Process and
  Molecular Function terms, and Reactome pathways are ranked by BioBERT semantic
  similarity to the Key Event; a curator assigns a confidence level through a
  structured rubric and an administrator approves each mapping before it enters the
  public REST API. Approved mappings are exportable as GMT, RDF/Turtle with curation
  provenance, CSV and JSON.
authors:
  - family-names: Martens
    given-names: Marvin
    orcid: https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2230-0840
    affiliation: Department of Translational Genomics, Maastricht University
version: 2.9.0
date-released: '2026-08-13'
license: GPL-2.0-only
repository-code: https://github.com/marvinm2/molAOP-builder
url: https://molaop-builder.vhp4safety.nl
keywords:
  - adverse outcome pathway
  - AOP
  - Key Event
  - WikiPathways
  - Gene Ontology
  - Reactome
  - toxicology
  - pathway analysis
  - BioBERT
  - curation
  - FAIR data
  - new approach methodologies
